  "description": "Subject: DCM2NIIX conversion settings for the upcoming DICOM batch  \n\nHi Team,  \n\nFor the upcoming run we will be processing a standard DICOM dataset (the input type is **dicom**). All conversion parameters have been set to their default, non\u2011transforming values: lossless scaling is **n**, Philips scaling is **y**, and the output files will be compressed NIfTI (compress_nifti\u202f=\u202f**y**). We are not merging 2\u2011D slices (merge2d\u202f=\u202f**n**) and we will keep each series in a separate file (single_file_mode\u202f=\u202f**n**) using the default filename pattern \u201c%f\u201d. No anonymization for BIDS is requested (anonymize_bids\u202f=\u202f**n**), and no BIDS side\u2011car files will be generated (bids_sidecar\u202f=\u202f**n**). Private text notes are disabled (text_notes_private\u202f=\u202f**n**) and cropping is off (crop\u202f=\u202f**n**). Errors will not be ignored (ignore_errors\u202f=\u202ffalse) and we will not attempt to decompress any compressed DICOM files (decompress_dicoms\u202f=\u202ffalse). The conversion will include all series (convert_only_series\u202f=\u202f**all**) and we will not produce 3\u2011D volumes (vol3D\u202f=\u202ffalse). Derived images are not ignored (ignore_derived\u202f=\u202f**n**) and coil combination is disabled (coil_combine\u202f=\u202ffalse).  \n\nLet me know if any of these settings need to be adjusted before we start.  \n\nBest,  \n[Your Name]"
